cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this census, please cite it.
title: "A prefix census of 3n+c and 5n+1 cycles, with one verified Collatz instance"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Frohman
    given-names: Benjamin Stanley
    email: frohmanbenjamin@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-7068-3718"
    alias: Investor0x
repository-code: "https://github.com/BenFrohman/3n-plus-c-cycle-census"
license: CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - Collatz
  - 3n+1
  - 3n+c
  - 5n+1
  - hailstone
  - computational number theory
abstract: >
  Computational prefix census of the maps 3n+c and 5n+1, the conjugacy
  C_{-c}(n)=-C_c(-n), and the verified instance T^{1348}(989345275647)=1.
  This is not a proof of the Collatz conjecture.
